  "id": "boardstiff",
  "neon": "#e8c46a",
  "note": "BOARD STIFF — four floors of rooms by the night, the week or the month, on Kiln Lane.\n\nThe tile's prose: every window on the upper floors has a different curtain and two have a blanket,\nand a card in the door glass lists the terms in a hand that got tired: NIGHTLY, WEEKLY, MONTHLY, NO\nGUESTS AFTER TEN, NO COOKING, NO EXCEPTIONS.\n\nSo the upper floors are a regular grid of nine windows under string courses, and each one is lit a\ndifferent colour and brightness; the two with blankets are the plain dark ones. The ground floor has\nthe door under a canopy with the terms card beside it and a lit lobby window. Grey quoins at the\ncorners and a cornice give it the outline of a once-respectable house. The fire escape is on the\nflank, and the roof carries a tank and the HOTEL sign.\n\nThe wall is `ty_negeq` brick. It was `ty_apt_a`, which is in the window-grid family, so the\ntexture painted a second set of lit windows beside the authored ones.",
  "pal": "ty_negeq",
